1
00:05:51,818 --> 00:05:57,818
Save the Vault. Tell the Story.

2
00:11:43,636 --> 00:11:49,636
Zappa is a music, documentary film directed by Alex Winter.

3
00:17:35,454 --> 00:17:41,454
With the help of more than 10,000 dedicated Zappa fans, this is the long-awaited definitive documentary project
of Alex Winter documenting the life and career of enigmatic groundbreaking rock star Frank Zappa.

4
00:23:27,272 --> 00:23:33,272
Alex also utilizes in this picture thousands of hours of painstakingly digitized videos,
photos, audio, writing, and everything in between from Zappa's private archives.

5
00:29:19,090 --> 00:29:25,090
These chronicles have never been brought to a public audience before, until now.

6
00:35:10,909 --> 00:35:16,909
Self (archive footage), played by Frank Zappa.

7
00:41:02,727 --> 00:41:08,727
Self - Played with Zappa 1987-1988, played by Mike Keneally.

8
00:46:54,545 --> 00:47:00,545
Self - Author, Former Member of the GTOs, played by Pamela Des Barres.

9
00:52:46,363 --> 00:52:52,363
Self - Newscaster for Action News (archive footage), played by Lonnie Lardner.

10
00:58:38,181 --> 00:58:44,181
Self - Frank Zappa's Sister (archive footage), played by Patrice Zappa.

11
01:04:30,000 --> 01:04:36,000
Self - Frank Zappa's Mother (archive footage), played by Rose Zappa.

12
01:10:21,818 --> 01:10:27,818
Zappa is an American documentary film about the musician Frank Zappa.

13
01:16:13,636 --> 01:16:19,636
Directed by Alex Winter, it was released on November 27, 2020.

14
01:22:05,454 --> 01:22:11,454
Frank Zappa (1940–1993) was an American composer, bandleader, and guitarist.

15
01:27:57,272 --> 01:28:03,272
Best known for writing and performing a large body of unconventional rock music
and releasing many albums, his work combined multiple music genres.

16
01:33:49,090 --> 01:33:55,090
He held iconoclastic views about music, the music
industry, and American culture and politics.

17
01:39:40,909 --> 01:39:46,909
The Zappa documentary tells the story of his life and career.

18
01:45:32,727 --> 01:45:38,727
Director Alex Winter had free access to Zappa's extensive archives.

19
01:51:24,545 --> 01:51:30,545
The film includes footage of performances by Zappa and his various bands, as
well as many interviews of people who knew or worked with him.

20
01:57:16,363 --> 01:57:22,363
In addition to Zappa himself, the interview subjects include Bruce Bickford, Pamela Des Barres, Bunk Gardner,
Mike Keneally, Scott Thunes, Ian Underwood, Ruth Underwood, Steve Vai, Ray White, and Gail Zappa.

21
02:03:08,181 --> 02:03:14,181
The film explores themes of composer, biography,
avant-garde, progressive rock, rock singer.
